  "id": "21",
  "name": "Manufacture of basic pharmaceutical products and pharmaceutical preparations",
  "section": "C",
  "summary": "Pharmaceutical companies describe AI across the value chain: target identification, generative molecule and antibody design, protein structure prediction and in silico screening in discovery; trial design, patient recruitment, digital twins and synthetic control arms in development; and pharmacovigilance, medical writing, HCP engagement and Pharma 4.0 manufacturing downstream. Filings name AI-native discovery partners and compute investments, and discuss regulators' positions on AI in drug development (FDA credibility framework, EMA reflection paper, EU GMP Annex 22, non-animal methods). Risks include unproven AI-derived candidates, health-data privacy, inventorship of AI-assisted inventions and validation of AI in GxP settings.",
